Invalid example programs, one case per program, in byte order of name.

Each case is a txtar file pair: <name>/main.tck holds the program and
<name>/expected the compiler's output for it, with the program's path
printed as <name>/main.tck. An empty <name>/no-final-newline file after the
pair means the program's last line has no newline. internal/invalid
documents the format; go test ./test -run TestInvalid checks every case, and
-update rewrites the expected sections.

-- arg-count/main.tck --
package main

func f() {
}

func main() {
    f("dropped")
}
-- arg-count/expected --
stage: typeck
---

arg-count/main.tck:7:5: error: f expects 0 argument(s), got 1
06 |	func main() {
07 |	    f("dropped")
   |	    ^~~~~~~~~~~~
08 |	}

